# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository, check out native.
# Without this, Windows checkouts round-trip CRLF into the index and git warns
# on every `add`. The repository is the canonical form; the working copy is not.
* text=auto

# Files that must be LF even on a Windows checkout — they are read by tools or
# shells that do not tolerate CR.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.ts        text eol=lf
# ── ADDED WITH apps/web, AND THE PUSH HOOK IS HOW THEY WERE FOUND ───────────
#
# `.tsx`, `.css` and `.html` fell through to `* text=auto` above, so a Windows
# checkout wrote them CRLF — and `.prettierrc` pins `endOfLine: lf`, which made
# `format:check` fail on ten files that had just passed before being committed.
#
# The failure is confusing in exactly the way this file's opening comment
# describes: nothing in the source changed, `prettier --write` "fixed" it, and
# the next checkout broke it again. The extensions have to be listed.
*.tsx       text eol=lf
*.css       text eol=lf
*.html      text eol=lf
*.js        text eol=lf
*.mjs       text eol=lf
*.cjs       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
*.dart      text eol=lf
.nvmrc      text eol=lf
.gitignore  text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.editorconfig  text eol=lf
.env.example   text eol=lf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
